{"conversation":"Thanks for explaining the greedy approach! It makes sense to pick boxes with the most units first. I will try to actually implement the sorting and then iterate through the boxes to load them until the truck is full or there are no more boxes left.","python_code":"class Solution:
    def maximumUnits(self, boxTypes: List[List[int]], truckSize: int) -> int:
        # Sort boxTypes by units per box in descending order
        boxTypes.sort(key=lambda x: x[1], reverse=True)
        total_units = 0
        for boxes, units in boxTypes:
            if truckSize == 0:
                break
            # Load as many boxes as possible
            boxes_to_load = min(boxes, truckSize)
            total_units += boxes_to_load * units
            truckSize -= boxes_to_load
        return total_units"}
